request@5dc35465
  the slot is reserved at request time and travels in the event, so the reply writes a parameter key and each invariant is checked key by key (a computed key is proven too since 2026-11-05, quantified, but needs nothing here)
  one request per source at a time keeps the public APIs from being hammered by a button-masher
  the 5-second cooldown is politeness toward free APIs with no key; 5 is a guess, not a published limit
store@141bc5af
  the reply carries src and slot back from the event, so one definition serves every source; store_joke and
  store_pun only shape each API's JSON (setup + punchline, or joke) into the one text store keeps
give_up@dd413476
  frees a source whose reply didn't arrive; written before S12, when nothing else did that. Now the host also calls fetch_failed once no reply has come by the deadline (portal.host, default 300 s), so give_up is the earlier, manual way
upvote@057c3699
  votes are anonymous: Kern has no identity for page visitors yet, so one person can vote many times
